# Endless Battle — Project Constraints

Before editing Endless Battle gameplay/runtime code, read:

1. `docs/GAME_CONSTITUTION.md`
2. `docs/ENGINE_RULES.md`
3. `docs/MOVEMENT_CONTRACT.md`
4. `docs/WORKFLOW.md`

These are **mandatory** project constraints. Source code is implementation truth; these docs are design/engineering law.

## Before modifying code — summarize internally

- Relevant ownership (e.g. `SelectionManager`, `MilitaryDirectorV2`, `ArmyCommanderV2`, `AIPlayerState`, `MatchCompositionRoot`, `PlayerRouteNavigation`)
- Forbidden regressions (stale commands, freed Nodes, parser breaks, unrelated system edits)
- Relevant system contract (especially player movement)

## Hard rules

- Do **not** layer new player movement on deprecated formation/corridor/follow-leader/stuck-stack mechanics — follow `MOVEMENT_CONTRACT.md`; use/extend `PlayerRouteNavigation`
- Latest player command always wins (command generation / tokens)
- Do **not** introduce raw stale Node ownership — prefer `EntityHandle` / instance IDs + `NodeSafety`
- Do **not** modify unrelated systems
- Run existing parse/headless validation after implementation
- Gameplay tasks require **manual user acceptance before commit** unless the user explicitly says otherwise
- Do not commit yet when the user has not asked
- UI reads state and issues requests; UI is never gameplay-state authority
